{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FJc6PqgQTLq23Et2Hd9hpa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-228 — Live-orphan taxonomy + ratchet for check_docs (repo-review-2026-07-18 M-07)\n2\t\n3\t**Branch:** dualplan-routing-fix · **Filed:** 2026-07-18 (review M-07) ·\n4\t**BuildTier:** medium · **SafetyClass:** ordinary (doc navigability tooling).\n5\t\n6\t## Why\n7\t\n8\t`check_docs` reports 48 live orphan warnings. Most are *retained evidence* —\n9\treviews, closed-WI specs, plan-round artifacts — that should stay live but\n10\tunlinked-from-navigation is the wrong frame for them; meanwhile genuinely\n11\tundiscoverable new docs hide in the same noise. Deleting or globally\n12\tignoring would destroy history; indexing everything would bloat navigation\n13\t(§0 table). The census only ever grows silently — the same failure mode\n14\tWI-225 ratchets for complexity.\n15\t\n16\t## Scope\n17\t\n18\t1. **Taxonomy.** Classify the 48 into declared classes (e.g.\n19\t   `review-evidence`, `closed-wi-spec`, `round-artifact`, `genuine-orphan`)\n20\t   recorded where check_docs can read them — a small declaration file or\n21\t   path-pattern rules in the script's config surface, whichever the script\n22\t   already supports more naturally. Genuine orphans get linked or indexed;\n23\t   evidence classes are *expected*-live-orphans and stop warning\n24\t   individually.\n25\t2. **Ratchet.** check_docs fails (or warns loudly under `--strict`) only on\n26\t   **newly introduced** live orphans outside the declared classes — baseline\n27\t   the residue, never fail history. Downstream behavior unchanged unless the\n28\t   adopter declares classes (default = today's behavior; the kit must not\n29\t   surprise existing repos).\n30\t\n31\t**Non-goals:** no doc deletions; no mass index page; no change to broken-link\n32\tsemantics.\n33\t\n34\t## Done-when\n35\t\n36\tThe 48 classified with zero unexplained residue (or each residue linked);\n37\tcheck_docs regression tests cover class declaration, expected-orphan\n38\tsuppression, and new-orphan failure; kit scripts stay stdlib-only; smoke bar\n39\tgreen per commit, full suite at close; `docs/status.md`/README untouched by\n40\tthe noise reduction (no navigation bloat).\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d4111ed-4ba5-4d25-9fec-acbdeb5debd4","uuid":"2ca85970-6292-4f3c-b848-7c6c6bcceb17","timestamp":"2026-07-18T22:06:34.677Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\1-g3-WI-228-a8da\\docs\\specs\\WI-228.md","content":"# WI-228 — Live-orphan taxonomy + ratchet for check_docs (repo-review-2026-07-18 M-07)\n\n**Branch:** dualplan-routing-fix · **Filed:** 2026-07-18 (review M-07) ·\n**BuildTier:** medium · **SafetyClass:** ordinary (doc navigability tooling).\n\n## Why\n\n`check_docs` reports 48 live orphan warnings. Most are *retained evidence* —\nreviews, closed-WI specs, plan-round artifacts — that should stay live but\nunlinked-from-navigation is the wrong frame for them; meanwhile genuinely\nundiscoverable new docs hide in the same noise. Deleting or globally\nignoring would destroy history; indexing everything would bloat navigation\n(§0 table). The census only ever grows silently — the same failure mode\nWI-225 ratchets for complexity.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. **Taxonomy.** Classify the 48 into declared classes (e.g.\n   `review-evidence`, `closed-wi-spec`, `round-artifact`, `genuine-orphan`)\n   recorded where check_docs can read them — a small declaration file or\n   path-pattern rules in the script's config surface, whichever the script\n   already supports more naturally. Genuine orphans get linked or indexed;\n   evidence classes are *expected*-live-orphans and stop warning\n   individually.\n2. **Ratchet.** check_docs fails (or warns loudly under `--strict`) only on\n   **newly introduced** live orphans outside the declared classes — baseline\n   the residue, never fail history. Downstream behavior unchanged unless the\n   adopter declares classes (default = today's behavior; the kit must not\n   surprise existing repos).\n\n**Non-goals:** no doc deletions; no mass index page; no change to broken-link\nsemantics.\n\n## Done-when\n\nThe 48 classified with zero unexplained residue (or each residue linked);\ncheck_docs regression tests cover class declaration, expected-orphan\nsuppression, and new-orphan failure; kit scripts stay stdlib-only; smoke bar\ngreen per commit, full suite at close; `docs/status.md`/README untouched by\nthe noise reduction (no navigation bloat).\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}}}
