{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kwustfp6UUQ1LyekBt2vw","type":"tool_result","content":"808f95d File WI-229: the M-05 spine migration, staged with an attestation hard stop\n657d346 WI-225: pin the C901 census with a per-function ratchet baseline\n413d49f File WI-225..228: consume review-18 H-02/M-06/M-07 + record the census drift\n6fd80d5 WI-224: preserve quoted round paths in salvage\n8bd3298 WI-223: ratify fail-closed SELECT disposition\n24f9551 WI-222: salvage committed round evidence on post-commit disposition resets\n660ddbd File WI-222 + WI-223 + WI-224: consume the WI-220 deep-review findings\n7981b2d WI-221: raise dual-plan round budget\n---STACK---\n# docs/stack.ini — the kit meta-repo's own product toolchain, declared once.\n#\n# The \"product\" this repo builds is the kit under project-trajectory/; its tests\n# live in tests/ (they bootstrap a real scaffold and exercise every script). This\n# is the meta-repo's SELF-adoption of the process it ships — IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md\n# Thread 47. scripts under project-trajectory/scripts/check.py read this file.\n\n[paths]\nsrc = project-trajectory/scripts\ntests = tests\n\n[product]\nformat = {py} -m ruff format --check {src} {tests}\nlint = {py} -m ruff check {src} {tests}\n# `-n auto` runs the suite across all cores via pytest-xdist (WI-075). Every test\n# is isolated in tmp_path and the meta-tree readers are read-only, so the suite is\n# xdist-safe; subprocess coverage (tests/conftest.augment_env) holds per-worker\n# (measured combined total 90.8%, unchanged from serial). Measured on a 24-core\n# box: ~377 s serial -> ~65 s parallel; the coverage step ~726 s -> ~157 s.\n# The `smoke` tier stays as declared; the coverage args below still apply.\ntest = {py} -m pytest -q -n auto\n\n[tiers]\nsmoke = -m smoke\nfull = -m \"not release\"\nrelease =\nall =\n\n[coverage]\n# Subprocess coverage IS wired (Thread 47 Phase 6). This suite exercises the kit\n# scripts as SUBPROCESSES (b