{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdAKCxBEYDVPwp6gw5X8H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-228 is complete and committed with the required trailers; the working tree is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\n**WI-228 — Live-orphan taxonomy + newly-introduced-orphan ratchet in `check_docs`** (SR-012), committed as `57fe091` on `llm/train/1-g3-WI-228-a8da`.\n\n**The problem (review-18 M-07):** `check_docs` emitted ~60 steady live-orphan warnings, mostly *retained evidence* (reviews, closed-WI specs, dual-plan artifacts) that should stay on disk but isn't a navigation node — so genuinely undiscoverable new docs hid in the noise, and the census only ever grew silently (the same failure mode WI-225 ratchets for complexity).\n\n**What I built:**\n- **Taxonomy** — a new declared-file surface `docs/<docs>/orphans-allow` (same census idiom as `docs/dupes-allow`/`docs/status-lint`): shell globs declaring *expected* live-orphan classes. A matched orphan is dropped from per-doc warnings (one aggregate `note` replaces them) and never a finding, even under `--strict-orphans`.\n- **Ratchet** — an orphan matching **no** declared class stays *genuine*: warns (fails under `--strict-orphans`) exactly as before. Absent file ⇒ today's behavior unchanged, so the kit never surprises an existing repo.\n- **Meta dogfood** — `docs/orphans-allow` classifies the repo's evidence to **zero unexplained residue**; the one genuine straggler (`specs/parallel-dispatch-design-notes.md`) is **linked** from its companion plan rather than listed. Verified: `--strict-orphans` on the meta tree now exits 0.\n\n**Engineering care:**\n- `main()` sat at C901 complexity exactly 10 — I extracted a `report_orphans` helper so it drops below the limit, keeping the WI-225 ratchet **baseline unchanged**.\n- The new `load_orphan_classes` reader duplicates the `status-lint` declared-reader idiom intra-file (sanctioned F5) — **censused** in `docs/dupes-allow` (not hoisted), like WI-132 before it.\n- `fnmatch` is stdlib; kit stays stdlib-only.\n- `docs/architecture.md` regenerated for the three new functions (generated code map) to keep the pre-commit floor green.\n\n**Verification (real output):** ruff format/lint clean · complexity ratchet green (census identical) · dupes gate green · 7 new regression tests (class declaration, expected-orphan suppression, warn/strict-fail ratchet, never-fail-under-strict invariant, unchanged broken-link semantics, load/partition units) · **full suite 1082 passed, 3 skipped** · pre-commit floor all-green.\n\n`docs/status.md`, `README.md`, `docs/log.md`, `work-items.csv` status cells, and coordination/dashboard artifacts were left untouched, per the worker contract.\n\nOne note for the integrator: the pre-commit `format` step **SKIPPED** because the git hook's system Python (3.12) can't import `ruff` — a pre-existing environment quirk (`run scripts/setup`), not a regression; I ran `ruff format --check` and `ruff check` independently and both passed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":178399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":858},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d4111ed-4ba5-4d25-9fec-acbdeb5debd4","uuid":"bedb1f8d-9946-4998-a81a-4e6047e3d060","request_id":"req_011CdAKCvKMtW9BDmajkHjP7"}
